## 3. Standard Operation Procedure (SOP-INF...)
## 3.1 Gold Image Initialization
Execute these tasks during your automated image creation pipelines (e.g., Packer, Azure Image Builder, or MDT task sequences) before sealing the OS.

Powershell
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    SOP Step: Automated Per-Machine OneDrive Installation
#>
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
# Terminate active runtime instances
Stop-Process -Name "OneDrive" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
# Eradicate legacy per-user setups to clear execution space
$UserSetup = "$env:LocalAppData\Microsoft\OneDrive\OneDriveSetup.exe"if (Test-Path $UserSetup) {
    Start-Process -FilePath $UserSetup -ArgumentList "/uninstall" -Wait -NoNewWindow
}
# Pull down the verified corporate deployment package
$InstallerPath = "$env:TEMP\OneDriveSetup.exe"
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://microsoft.com" -OutFile $InstallerPath
# Execute system-wide installation
$InstallResult = Start-Process -FilePath $InstallerPath -ArgumentList "/allusers", "/silent" -Wait -Passthruif ($InstallResult.ExitCode -ne 0) { throw "Installation failure with code $($InstallResult.ExitCode)" }

## 3.2 Compaction Engine Stamping
To ensure that profile containers shrink when files are unlinked, the native compaction engine must be stamped directly into the registry of the master image.

Powershell
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    SOP Step: FSLogix Storage Engine Optimization
#>
$FSLogixPath = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\FSLogix\Apps"if (-not (Test-Path $FSLogixPath)) { New-Item -Path $FSLogixPath -Force | Out-Null }
# Enable continuous background sector shrinking on logoff
Set-ItemProperty -Path $FSLogixPath -Name "VHDCompactDisk" -Value 1 -PropertyType DWord -Force

## 3.3 Active Directory Policy Deployments

# GPO 1: Developers & Quality Assurance (GPO-COMP-VDI-OneDrive-DevQA)
Link this object strictly to the Organizational Unit holding the VMware compute resource objects.

Loopback Processing: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > System > Group Policy
Setting: 
Configure user Group Policy Loopback Processing mode ➔ Enabled (Replace)

* Storage Optimization: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
Setting: Use OneDrive Files On-Demand ➔ Enabled
Setting: Prevent users from turning off Files On-Demand ➔ Disabled (Maintains developer velocity for local build targets)

* Automated Purging: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > System > Storage Sense
Setting: Allow Storage Sense ➔ Enabled
Setting: Configure Storage Sense Cloud Content dehydration ➔ Enabled (30 Days)


# GPO 2: Azure Consultants (GPO-COM-AVM-OneDrive-Consultants)
Link this object directly to the Organizational Unit housing the hybrid-joined Azure VMs.

* Loopback Processing: Set to Enabled (Replace) via the System Policy path.
* Storage Hardening: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
Setting: Use OneDrive Files On-Demand ➔ Enabled
Setting: Prevent users from turning off Files On-Demand ➔ Enabled (Enforces cloud-only layout; blocks local persistence)
Setting: Block syncing personal OneDrive accounts ➔ Enabled (Mitigates intellectual property leakage risks)

* Aggressive Purging: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > System > Storage Sense
Setting: Allow Storage Sense ➔ Enabled
Setting: Configure Storage Sense Cloud Content dehydration ➔ Enabled (3 Days)

* Identity Automation: User Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
Setting: Silently sign in users to OneDrive sync app with their Windows credentials ➔ Enabled (Leverages Entra ID PRT / Kerberos for invisible authentication matches)

* Loopback Processing: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > System > Group Policy
Setting: Configure user Group Policy Loopback Processing mode ➔ Enabled (Replace)

* Storage Optimization: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
Setting: Use OneDrive Files On-Demand ➔ Enabled
Setting: Prevent users from turning off Files On-Demand ➔ Disabled (Maintains developer velocity for local build targets)

Automated Purging: Computer Configuration > Policies > Administrative Templates > System > Storage Sense
Setting: Allow Storage Sense ➔ Enabled
Setting: Configure Storage Sense Cloud Content dehydration ➔ Enabled (30 Days)

## 4. Verification & Validation Protocol
Before promoting the newly deployed GPOs to production, Infrastructure engineers must execute the following validation matrix on a canary node:
1. Policy attainment test: Run gpresult /h gpreport.html from an elevated prompt. Verify that loopback processing matches the correct OU context and overrides standard user objects.
2. Binary Execution Verification: Open task Manager during an active user session. Verify that the running path for OneDrive.exe maps to C:\Program Files\Microsoft OneDrive\ and not the user's AppData directory.
3. Dehydration Constraint Test (Consultant Only): Access the synced OneDrive folder, right-click an item, and confirm that the choice "Always keep on this device" is greyed out or structurally missing from the context menu.
4. Security Boundaries Verification: Attempt to authenticate using an external Microsoft account (@outlook.com). The synchronization broker must immediately reject the handshake and throw an administrative block alert.

